<p><strong>Tools &amp; System Usage (Consolidated View)</strong></p>
<p>Key tools referenced:</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"bb25d44f-3526-437c-9156-eb1ed41bd8c2">NetRep (data valida=
tion, transaction history)</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"68e83d07-8e8e-4d05-ae28-bda9e80b918c">Compass (requests, =
processing)</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"43517b01-c4f1-4691-8dbd-cd95625c7a6d">iMOST (troubleshoot=
ing and exception handling)</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"ae86fd3c-c55e-4965-a931-ab484d6fc9b8">WebPanagon (tax sli=
ps)</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"28d6f7a1-b635-464e-b804-36a7d168a024">Croesus (historical=
 transaction data and coding)</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"7ea826e6-97ee-48a3-8ed4-c97408bd0602">PureFacts (fee proc=
essing)</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"9f61610e-678d-4c2a-a919-860019a4bdde">MAKO (account openi=
ng)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>User Access &amp; System Navigation</strong></p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"3d76958e-8bb8-4662-98a8-0b8d1158aaaa">Multiple user IDs a=
nd passwords across environments; up to 7=E2=80=938 per user. Includes Comp=
ass, NetRep, SZ, IB/PM platforms</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"2d9ed055-fbf3-4bfb-931e-bb332e0b0ed2">Need to log into mu=
ltiple environments (e.g., IB vs PM, multiple Compass/NetRep instances)</li=
>
 <li data-uuid=3D"e98e4b99-6514-4aea-b8e9-1cd7bd4d5433">Receive advisor ema=
ils from many email domains, must switch environments based on the email do=
main.</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"cba1e8aa-3af4-4853-85c4-674923e23787">Lack of unified/glo=
bal access across Harbourfront environments</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"a9e7a20c-fe2b-499f-b49f-1cccfd0ad9b7">Multiple platforms =
make it difficult to navigate, train, and document processes</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b7394bf1-14a4-477c-ab13-f73ca7f8f14a">Users must consult =
multiple systems to complete tasks (no =E2=80=9Cone-stop shop=E2=80=9D)</li=
>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1f345d3c-aeb3-4ab8-bb5d-b35cba44ef34">Internal workaround=
: teams created system/process reference matrix to guide usage</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Operational Workflow &amp; Processing Friction</strong></p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b99268c5-c7f0-4a03-9b1e-2b7832651fe2">High volume of advi=
sor escalations handled by operations</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d16a05cb-c991-4693-a105-6691bf5e3cfb">Significant effort =
spent on training and re-training users due to system complexity=20
  <ul>
   <li data-uuid=3D"43f69dbd-8a48-4bfd-8291-e7359c5cfc60">Example: The have=
 created an internal matrix for the branches to use to determine which plat=
form to use</li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"e024edb7-79d0-44e0-b09c-58ce9ce5cc72">Operations complete=
 processing in Servicing when needed.&nbsp; Usually when:=20
  <ul>
   <li data-uuid=3D"83b24097-5caa-4b1b-a8b3-5caf5477fad2">Advisor does not =
have access to RR codes. This occurs for cross-office transition of account=
s or recurring events created with a different RR code.&nbsp;</li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"99b00dce-fdb9-4723-8cc6-f0f7635f467a">Advisor is unable=
 to access system</li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"e212018b-ba60-4f86-bfcc-b0c5206c8ce0">Training/first ti=
me user; operations will show the advisor and guide them how to</li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"9d1bc3b8-59c7-428a-832c-6ee7fecd79a9">Ad hoc / exception-=
based processing required for certain requests (e.g., account opening check=
s, access gaps)</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"cc9bf6f3-be23-4aa1-be61-f102be61f260">Advisors sometimes =
bypass workflows (e.g., contacting trade desk directly)</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"MultiFirmUserDiscoveryHarbourfront-Enhancements">Enhancements&nbs=
p;</h2>
<p><strong>Bulk Processing &amp; Automation</strong></p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"5f5f772c-799e-4a0e-b13d-6f202e7c8dbc">PAC/SWP:=20
  <ul>
   <li>Need bulk setup capability</li>
   <li>Current process delayed by dependency on asset settlement</li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d96e99a7-8e02-4137-bce8-22324d5388ba">RIF/LIF:=20
  <ul>
   <li>Need bulk correction functionality</li>
   <li>Currently disconnected from account opening workflows</li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"7cbf43dc-9b9e-465c-8132-80b34249a685">MyPortfolio+ end in=
vestor access:=20
  <ul>
   <li>Bulk activation process is inconsistent and depends on account type<=
/li>
   <li>Process described as lengthy and disjointed</li>
  </ul></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Registered Account / Transaction Constraints</strong></p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"cdd85169-cc68-4e79-9e0c-ecf09a671b63">RESP limitations:=
=20
  <ul>
   <li>Must indicate cash account for withdrawals</li>
   <li>Plan-to-plan contributions not supported</li>
   <li>Compliance restrictions impact flows</li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"c53654c1-ae69-4f7c-b65e-3ce085d6deab"><strong>Registered =
account withdrawals may trigger errors (e.g., fee-related constraints requi=
ring iMOST</strong>)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Fees Processing&nbsp;</strong></p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"ec70f433-3611-44cc-835b-02c2b4710ee4">Complex fee ecosyst=
em.&nbsp;&nbsp;Multiple systems involved (PureFacts, AdminPro, NBIN fee tea=
m, Croesus)</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"e24a3d6e-350a-4cf3-9a53-7ac7e961fa94">Identified ineffici=
encies:=20
  <ul>
   <li>Multiple templates sent for fee processing (end-of-day batching)</li=
>
   <li>Opportunities to optimize AdminPro workflows</li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b01bb3e4-9c0a-49c3-958f-cea3b188b84a">ASC coding issues i=
mpacting account closing workflows</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Platform/User Experience</strong></p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"7b3b5b80-ecb0-4edf-bf5a-f1c326436de4">Strong demand for:=
=20
  <ul>
   <li>Platform consolidation (IB + PM environments)</li>
   <li>Unified access and workflows</li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"2f2a0d65-a7f2-40a4-a111-5d655fdfd5e2">Need for:=20
  <ul>
   <li>More intuitive system guidance</li>
   <li>Better training enablement and documentation support</li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"5d7d5bd1-efa8-4217-86c4-b36674e02ca5">Overall friction th=
emes:=20
  <ul>
   <li>Confusion driven by system fragmentation</li>
   <li>Training complexity driven by inconsistent processes</li>
  </ul></li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
<p><strong>Top 3 Challenges (System/Technology/Platform)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Lindsey</strong></p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d17775c5-1ded-40c7-a557-2f4723c8e0ee">Multiple logins are=
 very challenging - emails are coming in for all environments</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"be4b3d0d-6f11-4466-abba-c9572d635cc0">Look in different p=
laces for information is very confusing for advisors, training is challengi=
ng&nbsp; - should be a one stop shop</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Brandi</strong></p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"fd5e2f8f-249a-45af-9aa6-c81573b4b059">Too many systems - =
difficult to train and document processes</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"ded31531-9f0f-4d19-aea3-648e215ea711">Would like more inf=
ormative guidance</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Ivan</strong></p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"a445dac9-e3ab-43e9-8fa5-df7c3acdb157">Logins too many</li=
>
 <li data-uuid=3D"40804a41-1da1-4239-b5ab-f2e2720e7422">Updated platforms -=
 net rep looks old</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"93cde39c-d571-476f-a1c5-a51628d3e96b">Information in net =
rep&nbsp; - not always translated to acct&nbsp; 'successor holder' is in rr=
 comments TFSA acct</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Ian</strong></p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"eac8e192-e809-442f-af7f-9c3874f71921">Withdrawal - error =
message for fees withdrawal from registered acct - use imost</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"184ab5a1-9bb0-4144-897b-85b86d21fea7">Files to admin pro =
- sent for processing - what is this - could this be optimized - management=
 fees, final admin fee for acct closing - four templates sent at the end of=
 the day.&nbsp; Fee tool in r2 not being used - use purfacts</li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"panelHeader" style=3D"border-bottom-width: 1px;">
  <b>Meeting with Aaron Caughlhan</b>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"panelContent">
  <p class=3D"auto-cursor-target"><strong>June 17, 2026</strong></p>
  <p class=3D"auto-cursor-target">Attendees:&nbsp; Aaron Caughlan, Penny La=
m, Owen Mullings, Candi So, Susanne Clifford</p>
  <p><strong>Harborfront User Access Management Process:</strong></p>
  <p>Aaron from Harborfront provided Penny, Candi, Owen, and Susanne with a=
 comprehensive walkthrough of the end-to-end user access management process=
 for the NBIN platforms, detailing steps from new user onboarding, applicat=
ion provisioning, and account management to deactivation and ongoing access=
 reviews.</p>
  <ul>
   <li style=3D"list-style-type: none;">
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"91aa0046-2aa0-4c0b-a030-af3f169ca07a"><strong>Role an=
d Team Structure: </strong>Aaron explained that the user access function at=
 Harbourfront is primarily managed by themself, with Hassan Zafar as backup=
, and that the team falls under operations, reporting to Brent Gillis. They=
 are responsible for all user access requests across Harborfront, including=
 KJ, Rothenberg, and Wealth Council instances.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"7638b3bb-d83e-432a-8655-cde22e02777b"><strong>Onboard=
ing and Provisioning Workflow: </strong>The process begins with HR notifica=
tions for new hires, after which Aaron uses checklists and forms to determi=
ne required access, sets up calendar reminders, and prepares user access fo=
rms based on team type. Default applications are provisioned, and additiona=
l apps are added per branch request. System access documents with credentia=
ls are sent to users on their start date.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"73d768ff-fc92-43f3-8ecd-b19e503688e0"><strong>Applica=
tion and Account Management: </strong>Aaron maintains a master team list sp=
readsheet tracking all users, their R codes, registration status, and appli=
cation access. This list is used for both onboarding and ongoing management=
, allowing for efficient updates and reference for finance and auditing pur=
poses.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"91ff5d54-e2fe-440d-b445-88664c378a9a"><strong>Ticket =
Tracking and Efficiency: </strong>A ticket tracker spreadsheet is used to m=
onitor NBIN ticket submissions, ensuring visibility for both Aaron and Hass=
an, especially when one is away. This tracker helps manage pending requests=
 across multiple Harborfront instances and supports follow-up with NBIN as =
needed.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"e96cc683-d5bc-4e1c-9f9d-5e5e631118db"><strong>Modific=
ation and Attestation Processes: </strong>For existing users requesting add=
itional access, requests are submitted via email, and forms are used to doc=
ument and authorize changes. Compliance is involved in R code changes, with=
 approvals managed through Wave. Quarterly attestations are cross-checked a=
gainst the team list, though recent issues with SFTP access have hindered t=
imely reviews.<strong>Challenges and Issues in Access Management: </strong>=
Aaron discussed with Penny and Candi the main challenges faced in user acce=
ss management, including late or changing requests from managers, rare HR m=
odifications, and technical limitations in access review and attestation pr=
ocesses.=20
      <ul>
       <li data-uuid=3D"29b0d8e2-6cfe-4e41-b4d5-230a09cfa5c0"><strong>Chang=
ing Access Requirements: </strong>Occasionally, managers request changes to=
 user access after initial setup, requiring Aaron to disable or adjust appl=
ication access, which creates extra work. HR modifications after onboarding=
 are rare but can also necessitate quick corrections.</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"ce8a17e1-435b-46c1-893b-ce435b167aad"><strong>Techn=
ical Limitations in Attestation: </strong>Quarterly attestation lists from =
NBIN are only available via SFTP, which Aaron and the IT team have had trou=
ble accessing, leading to missed or delayed reviews. Aaron requested that N=
BIN consider alternative delivery methods, but security policies prevent th=
is.</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"6975f1b8-b571-4f99-9fb4-98a1e05f8307"><strong>Effic=
iency and Documentation Gaps: </strong>The need for manual tracking and rec=
onciliation between Harbourfront's internal lists and NBIN's records is tim=
e-consuming, especially when integrating new teams or handling large number=
s of codes and users.</li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul></li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Access Review, Deactivation, and Compliance Oversight: </stron=
g></p>
  <p>Penny and Aaron reviewed the ongoing processes for access custodianshi=
p, including regular updates to the team list, deactivation procedures, com=
pliance involvement in R code management, and the use of quarterly attestat=
ions for oversight.</p>
  <ul>
   <li style=3D"list-style-type: none;">
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"5ee059fd-c136-4127-8fa1-60bb96d43e37"><strong>Ongoing=
 Access Review: </strong>Aaron is responsible for ensuring that only approp=
riate users retain access, updating the team list as people join or leave, =
and cross-checking against quarterly attestation lists, though these are so=
metimes out of date.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"ad289f53-73e8-4c39-84a4-c97f74b4b84e"><strong>Deactiv=
ation Procedures: </strong>Departures are managed with calendar reminders, =
and all application access is deactivated on the scheduled date. If discrep=
ancies arise, they are typically identified by managers or through periodic=
 reviews.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"13f7b161-9957-45e7-9fdd-ef76177abc83"><strong>Complia=
nce and RR Code Management: </strong>Compliance is involved in R code chang=
es, with requests processed through Wave and approvals required from both c=
ompliance and finance. Aaron maintains bulk templates for efficient updates=
 and auditing.</li>
    </ul></li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Integration and Consolidation of Acquired Firms: </strong></p>
  <p>Owen and Aaron discussed the ongoing integration of acquired firms lik=
e KJ Harrison and Rothenberg, the continued role of legacy user access cont=
acts, and the challenges and opportunities in consolidating user access man=
agement across instances.</p>
  <ul>
   <li style=3D"list-style-type: none;">
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"df20542a-aeb2-4b09-a118-62433ad63c82"><strong>Legacy =
User Access Roles: </strong>Aaron confirmed that legacy user access contact=
s at acquired firms still handle some tasks, but Harborfront encourages cen=
tralization of application-specific requests to streamline processes and av=
oid overlap.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"4376be65-7746-4267-8a79-bb3f77c735ba"><strong>Consoli=
dation Challenges: </strong>Differences in access models, such as firm acce=
ss settings and onboarding profiles, present challenges for merging user ma=
nagement across instances. For example, KJ Harrison requires explicit code =
listings for firm access, unlike other instances.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"4f9087fe-d69b-4fcf-97dd-016ea518c784"><strong>Opportu=
nities for Unified Management: </strong>Aaron and the team see value in con=
solidating user access management, which would provide greater visibility a=
nd efficiency, though technical and procedural discrepancies must be addres=
sed.</li>
    </ul></li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Requests for Process Improvements and Documentation: </strong>=
Aaron requested from Penny, Candi, and Owen clearer documentation and proce=
ss improvements, particularly regarding role definitions, access rights, an=
d technical behaviors in Compass and related systems, to support the upcomi=
ng consolidation and ongoing management.</p>
  <ul>
   <li style=3D"list-style-type: none;">
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"8a2755a0-fb23-43eb-8364-51556bbaddb9"><strong>Clarifi=
cation of Role Behaviors: </strong>Aaron asked for a robust breakdown of wh=
at each role and access option in Compass and related systems actually enab=
les, noting that current guides do not always account for observed behavior=
s or exceptions.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"279db76d-9f3e-4240-8e8b-05345e32df8c"><strong>Process=
 and System Enhancements: </strong>Aaron highlighted the need for more intu=
itive access toggling in Secured Zone, improved notification for attestatio=
n file availability, and better support for bulk updates and integration sc=
enarios.</li>
    </ul></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Follow-up tasks:</p>
  <ul>
   <li data-uuid=3D"c33bdd1b-1714-46e4-a059-f457294f616e"><strong>KJ Instan=
ce Firm Access Behavior: </strong>Verify the existing behavior for firm acc=
ess setup in the KJ instance and clarify if blank fields can now be used wi=
thout errors. (Penny, Candi)</li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"58b120c9-73df-4778-8871-459e0b81a2c2"><strong>Onboardin=
g Profile Role Discrepancies: </strong>Investigate and clarify the discrepa=
ncies in onboarding profile roles across Harbourfront, Rothenberg, and KJ i=
nstances, and provide feedback to Aaron.&nbsp;</li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"066a0c60-20bd-4eba-b2e5-00ad6267354f"><strong>Compass R=
ole and Access Guide: </strong>Provide an updated and robust breakdown of C=
ompass roles and access options, including clarification on mutual fund upl=
oad visibility and any role-specific access nuances.</li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"aad1216a-b788-4545-b79d-51b4da25375e"><strong>Quarterly=
 Attestation File Access: </strong>Resolve the issue with SFTP access for q=
uarterly attestation files and ensure user access team is looped in on noti=
fication emails when files are posted.&nbsp;</li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"69086c88-65f9-4be3-8095-aec5ed79d042"><strong>Integrati=
on of Master Lists from Acquired Firms: </strong>Integrate Rothenberg and K=
J master lists and bulk spreadsheets for statements and transfer notificati=
ons into Harborfront=E2=80=99s consolidated tracking system.</li>
  </ul>
 </div>
</div>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
    </div>
</body>
